<!--
  RUN, drawn as paths rather than text so the icon never depends on a font being installed and
  cannot reflow.

  The letterforms follow PT Mono: monospaced, square, mechanical. Every glyph gets the same advance
  of 15.75, so the three sit on a fixed pitch rather than being optically spaced. That squareness is
  the whole difference from an earlier rounded geometric pass, which read as friendly when this
  should read as an instrument.

  Three details are load-bearing.

  Outer edges, not centrelines, drive the geometry. Cap height (45) and baseline (63) are stated
  once and every vertex derives from them, because a mitred corner sits half a stroke inside the
  outer edge while a butt cap sits on it. An earlier pass put all three letters on one centreline
  and the U came out short of its neighbours.

  The N's diagonal is a separate subpath, not a corner of the stems. A mitre at that acute angle
  throws a spike well past the cap height, and a bevel or round join cuts the stem short instead.
  Held as its own stroke, its angled caps tuck entirely inside the square stems and the outer
  silhouette stays exactly rectangular.

  The R's leg is a filled quad rather than a stroke. A stroke's cap is always perpendicular to its
  own direction, so a diagonal leg gets an angled terminal, and every other terminal in this mark is
  a flat horizontal or vertical cut. Filled, it ends square on the baseline and flush with the
  letter's right edge. Its top edge sits inside both the stem and the bowl's bottom bar, so the join
  never shows. For the same reason the bowl turns with rounded corners rather than mitres: that is
  the corner the U already uses, and the R was the one letter not speaking it.

  The launcher shows a circle of radius 36 from the centre, not the full 108 canvas and not the
  66dp square usually quoted. This mark reaches 24.2 at its worst corner, leaving 11.8 of clearance
  under every mask. A route-line design tried first measured 39.9 and clipped on every device.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- R: stem and bowl. The bowl turns with the same 3-radius corners as the U's bottom. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M33.75,63 L33.75,47.25 L39.75,47.25 A3,3 0 0 1 42.75,50.25 L42.75,52.125 A3,3 0 0 1 39.75,55.125 L33.75,55.125"
        android:strokeColor="#FF7A00"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="butt"
        android:strokeLineJoin="miter" />
    <!-- R: the leg, filled rather than stroked so its terminal is flat on the baseline. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32.65,55.5 L38.57,55.5 L45,63 L39.08,63 Z"
        android:fillColor="#FF7A00" />
    <!-- U: straight sides into a flat bottom with small corners, not a semicircle. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M49.5,45 L49.5,57.75 A3,3 0 0 0 52.5,60.75 L55.5,60.75 A3,3 0 0 0 58.5,57.75 L58.5,45"
        android:strokeColor="#FF7A00"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="butt"
        android:strokeLineJoin="miter" />
    <!-- N: two square stems and a diagonal held separately, so no join distorts the silhouette. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M65.25,63 L65.25,45 M74.25,45 L74.25,63 M65.25,46.5 L74.25,61.5"
        android:strokeColor="#FF7A00"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="butt"
        android:strokeLineJoin="miter" />
</vector>
